<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. John's, Newfoundland and Labrador</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St. John's is a port city on the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avalon-peninsula">Avalon Peninsula</a>, one of the oldest English settlements in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> and a base of the English cod fishery. It was repeatedly attacked in the Anglo-French wars; in the winter of 1696–1697 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-le-moyne-diberville">Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</a> marched from French Plaisance and destroyed it. It is now the capital of Newfoundland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/labrador">Labrador</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-johns-newfoundland-and-labrador.jpg" alt="St. John's, Newfoundland and Labrador" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quintin Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St._John%27s,_Newfoundland_and_Labrador_aerial_view_of_downtown_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
